## Causal Factors

The scenario's causal factors, under local `source_handle` values. Each one
gives its source type, the source's description, the factor's description in
this scenario, and whether code fills its `process_model_variable` or you
choose it. Give each listed factor one entry under its `source_handle`. Do not
return structural IDs.{% if has_feedback_authority %}

A feedback factor may carry `authority_for_update`, the recorded assessment of
whether its source is entitled to establish the value of the variable it
updates, as opposed to only reporting it: `authoritative`, `non_authoritative`,
`conditional` (only within the scope or conditions its `basis` states), or
`unknown`, with the `basis` that cites the supplied evidence. A factor without
it is unknown. When the source is non-authoritative, the flawed belief can be
that what the source reported establishes the value, such as taking a reported
approval as the approval itself.{% endif %}

